Subject: [PATCH 411/488] Sink detector: the drafter-row cut and its restore as
 TileLang kernels

The cut ran about ten eager torch kernels a greedy step (zeros, index_put,
gather, sub, and, where, gather, scatter) and the restore a scatter. One
kernel, a thread a row, masks the same drafts and keeps the same logits
and columns; the restore writes them back. Declared for the raw and
processed logits' dtypes and the FP32 vocabulary shard. A new test pins
the cut against the torch reference on full logits and on a shard, in
FP32 and BF16.
